ES:
{{TAG:0003:0004:}}Voy a pasar todo el día recogiendo
{{TAG:0000:0003:0200}}plumas{{TAG:0000:0003:FFFF}}.{{TAG:0007:0001:}} {{TAG:0003:0001:}}¿Por qué no pillas alguna?{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
¡Están por todas partes!

IT:
{{TAG:0003:0004:}}Oggi andrò a caccia di piume.{{TAG:0007:0001:}}{{TAG:0003:0001:}}
Vedessi quante ce ne sono!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
È il vento che le trasporta!

DE:
{{TAG:0003:0004:}}Heute werde ich {{TAG:0000:0003:0200}}Federn{{TAG:0000:0003:FFFF}} sammeln.{{TAG:0007:0001:}}
{{TAG:0003:0001:}}Die fliegen hier einfach so rum, also
schnapp dir doch auch ein paar!

IT:
{{TAG:0003:000F:}}Guarda un po',{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}} {{TAG:0005:0008:}}!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Sembriamo due gemelli!{{TAG:0000:0004:}}{{TAG:0003:0005:}}Il Carnevale è spassosissimo
perché ci si può travestire,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
{{TAG:0005:0007:}}!
Se uno non si traveste,
che Carnevale è?

TRANSLATION:
{{TAG:0003:0015:}}{{TAG:0000:0003:0400}}Pavé{{TAG:0000:0003:FFFF}} dans işini harbiden
biliyor!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Kalçaları kasırgadan hızlı
dönüyor,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
{{TAG:0005:0007:}}!

IT:
{{TAG:0003:0020:}}Oggi è {{TAG:0000:0003:0200}}Carnevale{{TAG:0000:0003:FFFF}}, {{TAG:0005:0007:}}!{{TAG:0007:0000:28000000}}{{TAG:0003:002A:}}
A Carnevale ogni abbuffata vale!
{{TAG:0003:0027:}}Mmmh, forse il detto non era così...

EN:
Dancing sure works up an appetite.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
{{TAG:0003:000B:}}I wonder if you could eat
{{TAG:0005:0013:0000}} while shaking it.

ES:
Te lo juro: bailar me da un hambre
de león. ¡Me comería hasta un árbol
con corteza y todo!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
{{TAG:0003:000B:}}Mmm... Igual me las puedo apañar
para comer {{TAG:000E:0002:}}{{TAG:0005:0013:0000}}
mientras me marco un buen baile.

FR:
Danser, ça m'ouvre l'appétit !{{TAG:0000:0004:}}{{TAG:0003:000B:}}Je me demande si je pourrais
manger {{TAG:000E:0002:}}{{TAG:0005:0013:0000}}
tout en remuant mon popotin...

DE:
Tanzen macht hungrig...{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
{{TAG:0003:000B:}}Ob ich es schaffe, dabei 'ne Portion
{{TAG:0005:0010:0000}} zu naschen?

TRANSLATION:
Dans insanı acıktırıyor.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
{{TAG:0003:000B:}}Acaba sallana sallana
{{TAG:0005:0013:0000}} yenir mi?

EN:
{{TAG:0003:0021:}}Don't I look cool{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} today?{{TAG:0007:0000:28000000}}
{{TAG:0003:0004:}}I got all decked out for {{TAG:0000:0003:0200}}Festivale{{TAG:0000:0003:FFFF}},
and I feel like a whole new me!

DE:
{{TAG:0003:0021:}}Seh ich heute nicht total cool aus?{{TAG:0007:0000:28000000}}
{{TAG:0003:0004:}}Äh,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}} he he he...{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} Ich hab mich extra für
{{TAG:0000:0003:0200}}Karneval{{TAG:0000:0003:FFFF}} so fein gemacht!

TRANSLATION:
{{TAG:0003:0021:}}Bugün havalı görünmüyor muyum{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}?{{TAG:0007:0000:28000000}}
{{TAG:0003:0004:}}{{TAG:0000:0003:0200}}Festivale{{TAG:0000:0003:FFFF}} için baştan aşağı
hazırlandım; resmen başka biriyim!

FR:
{{TAG:0003:0005:}}Aujourd'hui, c'est carnaval !{{TAG:0007:0000:28000000}}
Qu'est-ce qu'on attend pour aller
danser ?!

ES:
{{TAG:0003:002A:}}Oye, pues a lo tonto le voy cogiendo
el tranquillo a esto del bailoteo,{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
¿no te parece?

FR:
{{TAG:0003:002A:}}Je crois que plus ça va, plus mon
pas de danse s'améliore !{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
T'es pas d'accord ?

DE:
Tja...{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} Ich glaube,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}{{TAG:0003:002A:}} langsam werde
ich etwas besser beim Tanzen.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Was denkst du?

EN:
{{TAG:0003:0001:}}Things look pretty crazy outside. {{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
I'm gonna go get my dance on later,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
{{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

IT:
{{TAG:0003:0001:}}Caspitina! Hai visto che confusione
c'è là fuori?{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} Dopo mangiato,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
mi unirò anch'io ai festeggiamenti!

TRANSLATION:
{{TAG:0003:0001:}}Dışarısı epey çılgın görünüyor. {{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Birazdan ben de dans etmeye
çıkarım,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
{{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

EN:
{{TAG:0003:0003:}}If you're tired out from dancing,{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
take a break in my house, 
{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}{{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

DE:
Wenn man an Karneval drinnen
bleibt, ist es fast unheimlich ruhig,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
{{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

EN:
{{TAG:0003:0009:}}Dancing isn't for the faint of heart.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Taking that first step takes a lot
of guts, {{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}{{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

ES:
{{TAG:0003:0009:}}El baile no es para cobardes.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
¡Hace falta tener narices para
dar el primer paso, {{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}{{TAG:0005:0007:}}!

IT:
{{TAG:0003:0009:}}Ballare non è roba da pappemolli!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Per lasciarsi andare sulla pista
ci vuole fegato, {{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}{{TAG:0005:0007:}}!

DE:
{{TAG:0003:0009:}}Tanzen ist nichts für Angsthasen.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Man muss ganz schön mutig sein, um
den ersten Tanzschritt zu wagen!

TRANSLATION:
{{TAG:0003:0009:}}Dans korkak işi değil.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
İlk adımı atmak bile cesaret
ister, {{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}{{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

{{TAG:0003:0017:}}{{TAG:0000:0003:0200}}Festivale{{TAG:0000:0003:FFFF}} günü ne yenir acaba?{{TAG:0000:0004:}}{{TAG:0003:002B:}}
En iyisi bir sürü şey deneyip
hangisi işe yarıyor bakmak.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Hehehe!

EN:
{{TAG:0003:0005:}}I can't remember a morning that's
been as busy as this one.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} {{TAG:0000:0003:0200}}Festivale{{TAG:0000:0003:FFFF}}
is such a raucous holiday.

IT:
{{TAG:0003:0005:}}Non ricordavo una mattinata così
frenetica da un sacco di tempo!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Che festa caotica il Carnevale!

TRANSLATION:
{{TAG:0003:0005:}}Bu kadar hareketli bir sabahı
hatırlamıyorum.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} {{TAG:0000:0003:0200}}Festivale{{TAG:0000:0003:FFFF}}
gerçekten gürültülü bir bayram.

ES:
Ya se está haciendo de noche.{{TAG:0007:0000:28000000}}
Al Carnaval debe de quedarle nada
y menos entonces,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}} {{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

FR:
Il commence à faire sombre dehors.{{TAG:0007:0000:28000000}}
Le carnaval touche à sa fin,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
{{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

DE:
Es wird dunkel...{{TAG:0007:0000:28000000}} Dann geht der
{{TAG:0000:0003:0200}}Karneval{{TAG:0000:0003:FFFF}} wohl langsam zu Ende,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
{{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

IT:
{{TAG:0003:0009:}}Se non ti va, non voglio obbligarti,{{TAG:0007:0000:28000000}}{{TAG:0003:0001:}}
ma magari ci riprovo più tardi,
{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}{{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

DE:
{{TAG:0003:0009:}}Da kann man wohl nichts machen.{{TAG:0007:0000:28000000}}
{{TAG:0003:0001:}}Ich frag dich vielleicht später noch
mal, {{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}{{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

ES:
¡Qué idea se me acaba de ocurrir!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
¡Vamos a jugar a un juego de
Carnaval!{{TAG:0000:0004:}}{{TAG:0003:0001:}}Si ganas tú, {{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}te regalo una pluma.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Si gano yo,{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} {{TAG:0003:0006:}}¡me das tú una a mí!{{TAG:0007:0001:}}
{{TAG:0003:0005:}}¿Qué te parece?{{TAG:0007:0000:28000000}} ¡Vamos, vamos!{{TAG:000F:0005:15002800}}
Venga
Paso

